# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The cold start: the IDE is launched with NO project anywhere, and a
# person makes one from nothing -- a project, then a file in it, then
# words in the file -- through the shell's own panels, without touching
# a terminal.  Every earlier proof planted a project first, which is
# how an IDE that could not create anything went unnoticed.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
menu-pick TikuIDE
wait 25
note the application arrives announcing itself: its name, over its own
note mark, in a window that stands in front and then leaves on its own
expect-title TikuIDE
wait 200
expect-no-title TikuIDE
expect-title Project
note the menu offers the start: a new project, made where the person
note says, through the shell's own Save panel
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu New Project…|Open Project…|New File…|Add File…
menu-pick New Project…
wait 40
expect-title Save
note the panel offers the name the opener looks for; taking it as
note offered puts the project in the home the panel shows
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Save
note the description exists now, named for the folder that holds it
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/project.tiku title trk_home
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/project.tiku group Sources
note a new file, offered as BASIC because that is what boards speak
click-window Project
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick New File…
wait 40
expect-title Save
click 675 413
wait 90
note the file is IN the project -- appended to the description, so the
note lines this build does not know would have survived the edit
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/project.tiku file untitled.bas
note and its editor window is already open, ready to be typed into
expect-title untitled.bas
note with the caret standing at the head of the empty page: a person
note must SEE where their typing will land, and on an empty page any
note ink at all is the caret
expect-pixel 541 182 000000
key h shift
key i
wait 10
note the toolbar's Save is the same gesture as the menu's, one reach
note closer to the hand
click 560 155
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/untitled.bas Hi
note and the page is the person's to grow: the corner is dragged, the
note editor hears its new size and repaints at it: the grown ground is
note the PAGE's own paper, which only the application's repaint lays --
note a runtime filling the gap would leave panel grey there
press 990 440 1
wait 4
move 990 560 1
wait 4
release 990 560 1
wait 80
expect-pixel 700 500 ffffff
note asking for a NEW project where one already stands means opening
note it: a person naming an existing project is not asking to empty it
click-window Project
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick New Project…
wait 40
expect-title Save
note the panel notices the name is taken and asks; answering Replace is
note what hands the path over, and even THEN the project is opened
note rather than emptied -- the description still holds its file
click 675 413
wait 20
expect-alert exists
key r
wait 60
expect-no-title Save
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/project.tiku file untitled.bas
note the Window menu knows the window, as it knows every editor
click-window Project
wait 8
click 132 8
wait 8
expect-menu untitled.bas
menu-pick untitled.bas
wait 30
expect-title untitled.bas
note and a folder that does not exist yet is made without leaving the
note panel: the name field names the folder, New folder steps inside,
note and the offered name comes back, ready to save
click-window Project
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick New Project…
wait 40
expect-title Save
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key b
key l
key i
key n
key k
key e
key r
wait 6
click 410 413
wait 30
click 675 413
wait 80
note the project lives in the folder that was made for it, named for
note it -- and the one already in the home is untouched
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/blinker/project.tiku title blinker
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/project.tiku file untitled.bas
